        "step": 3,
        "description": "Bound the factor (x+1)²",
        "details": "Assume |x - 2| < 1, so 1 < x < 3, meaning 2 < x+1 < 4. Therefore, (x+1)² < 16."
      },
      {
        "step": 4,
        "description": "Combine the bounds",
        "details": "If |x - 2| < 1, then |f(x) - f(2)| = |x-2|·(x+1)² < 16|x-2|."
      },
      {
        "step": 5,
        "description": "Choose δ based on ε",
        "details": "For any ε > 0, set δ = min(1, ε/16). Then |x - 2| < δ implies |f(x) - f(2)| < 16·(ε/16) = ε."
      },
      {
        "step": 6,
        "description": "Conclude the proof",
        "details": "Since for every ε > 0, there exists δ > 0 such that |x - 2| < δ implies |f(x) - f(2)| < ε, the function f is continuous at x = 2."
      }
